{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 84}
{lyrics_rights: public-domain}
{genre: Traditional, Folk, Ballad}
{source: Traditional English ballad.}
{start_of_verse}
Are you [Em]goin[g] to [C]Scarborough [G]Fair
[Em]Parsley, sage, [C]rosemary and [D]thyme
[Em]Remember me to [C]one who [D]lives there
[Em]She once was a [C]true love of [D]mine
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse2}
Tell her to [Em]make me a [C]pair of [G]brocade
[Em]Of the [C]silvery [D]mercury and [Em]gold
Tell her to [C]find me a [G]pair of [D]shoes
And [Em]three dozen [C]lilies of [D]white
{end_of_verse2}
